  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Molecular Dynamics simulations can be used to study the size-dependent thermal response of FeCuCrCoNi high-entropy-alloy nanoparticles.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Root mean square displacement and radial distribution function can be used to analyze the thermal response of these nanoparticles.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The investigated FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticles have diameters ranging from 2 to 10 nm.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The simulations use a Nose-Hoover thermostat.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The simulations use a time step of 1 fs.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The temperature is varied from 300 to 1000 K in increments of 100 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Each simulation runs for 1 ns.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three replicates are performed at every temperature and particle-size point.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three replicates at each condition ensure statistical reliability.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atomic thermal vibration and diffusion increase with temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Atomic thermal vibration and diffusion become greater as nanoparticle size decreases because smaller particles have a higher surface-to-volume ratio.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enhanced thermal vibration and diffusion reduce the thermal stability of smaller FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticles.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thermal stability decreases as FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticle size decreases.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 500 K, a 2 nm FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticle has a predicted root mean square displacement of 0.25 nm.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 500 K, a 10 nm FeCuCrCoNi nanoparticle has a predicted root mean square displacement of 0.20 nm.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 500 K, bulk FeCuCrCoNi has a root mean square displacement of 0.15 nm.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Significant thermal-stability changes are theoretically predicted within the 2-10 nm size range.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2-10 nm range spans a transition from surface-dominated behavior to bulk-like behavior.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The numerical root mean square displacement values may depend on simulation parameters and variability in nanoparticle structures.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
